 "story": {
  "title": "The flood under the trees",
  "lede": "Edouard dropped more than 18 inches of rain on East Texas in early September 2026. Village Creek, which winds through the forests near Kountze, rose to 22 feet.",
  "body": [
   "Water under a forest canopy is invisible to optical satellites. L-band reaches the ground: its pulse bounces off the water, up the trunks and straight back to the radar. HH jumps while HV barely moves. That is the Bounce.",
   "On the September 3 pass, in the middle of the storm, 3,572 forested hectares in this box jumped 3 dB or more in HH while their HV held still. Twelve days later only 266 were still bouncing: the water had drained."
  ],
